A||||16||Patrick's Dad||What to you and your significant other argue about?||||2||
Z||000000||Patrick's Dad||12-21-2001||01:22 PM||||Not the heavy duty stuff, but what do you and your wife/hubby/girlfriend/boyfriend fight about most?<P>With us, it's music. I'm getting into the Bebop stuff (Miles, Coltrane, Dizzy & Bird). My wife likes Madonna, Duran Duran, and other '80's stuff (For the record, Prince is my big '80's thing). She can't stand Jazz.||||reg||2
Z||000001||wkayl||12-21-2001||01:46 PM||||Neatness and perfection.  My wife can't stand anything out of place. My garage drives her crazy.  Also if I make any craft items she inspects them for any imperfections.  I made a CU Bolder thing for my son for Christmas and I had to paint it 3 times to get the correct color of yellow.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/buffalo.jpg"> <BR>The yellow in the picture wouldn't have passed.  The flash on the camera makes it look more yellow than gold.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||12-21-2001||01:51 PM||||We don't argue much (thank God).  But we "bicker" a little about keeping the house clean, picking up after yourself, and stuff like washing the dish when you're done using it so they don't pile up.  Other than that... not much. Sometimes (especially around the holidays) we "bicker" about who's parent's house we're going to (Thanksgiving is usually the worst- Christmas is OK thanks to different "traditional" celebration days). <B>I love my wife.</B>  Just thought I'd add that for some reason (not that she ever reads the forum -unless I suggest something specific).<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||thomas_l||12-21-2001||01:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by wkayl:<BR><B>Neatness and perfection.  My wife can't stand anything out of place. My garage drives her crazy.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Same here. She calls my basement office space a fire hazard. As far as the garage is concerned, that to me is like her kitchen is to her. In the garage, there's room for her car and a clear path to the door. Likewise, I can get water and make coffee without disturbing the neatness in the kitchen. Quid pro quo  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
